@startuml
title net workspace architecture (current through RN8 N4)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
left to right direction

package "apps / preview integration" {
  [Runenwerk Editor Preview Client] as preview_client
  [Runtime Preview Host] as preview_host
}

package "engine integration" {
  [Application / Session Lifecycle] as engine_session
  [RunenNet Session Projection] as session_projection
  [Owner / Routing Projection] as owner_routing
  [Replication + Prediction Systems] as engine_replication
  [Replication I/O Staging] as engine_io
  [Replay Systems] as engine_replay
}

package "external RunenNet" {
  [runen-net Core] as runennet_core
  [runen-net-quic] as runennet_quic
}

package "net (remaining Runenwerk migration evidence)" {
  package "engine_sim" {
    [simulation vocabulary] as sim
  }

  package "engine_net" {
    [snapshot / ack / input envelopes] as net_protocol
    [live replication / input contracts] as net_replication
    [declarative replication metadata] as net_authoring
  }

  package "engine_net_macros" {
    [network authoring macros] as net_macros
  }

  package "engine_history" {
    [replay / archive / validation] as history
  }
}

preview_client --> runennet_quic : preview control client
preview_host --> runennet_quic : preview control server
runennet_quic --> runennet_core

engine_session --> runennet_core : negotiation + session lifecycle
engine_session --> session_projection : accepted bindings only
session_projection --> owner_routing
session_projection --> engine_replication : authorized ConnectionHandle set
engine_replication --> net_replication
engine_io --> net_protocol
engine_replay --> history

net_replication --> runennet_core : ConnectionHandle identity
net_replication --> sim
net_authoring --> net_replication
history --> sim
net_macros --> net_authoring

note right of runennet_core
Standalone RunenNet is the sole reusable
connection/session/delivery/replication/prediction
semantic authority.
end note

note right of session_projection
Iterable engine projection only.
It does not authorize lifecycle mutations.
end note

note right of net_replication
engine_net is temporary live migration evidence.
Dead runtime commands/events, synthetic transport lanes,
and snapshot-payload prediction scaffolding are gone.
end note

note right of engine_io
Engine work queues stage retained messages.
Queue admission is not RunenNet DeliveryAcceptance.
end note

note right of runennet_quic
Concrete QUIC exists for the already-migrated
preview channel. The engine has no generic transport adapter.
end note

@enduml
